    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28095" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δορπία</span></b> , ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>the first day of the feast
				Apaturia,</i> celebrated by public suppers in each phratria,
			personified in <i><span class="en">
				Philyll.
				8.2
			</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρόπεμπτα τῆς Δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					2.841b62
				</span></i>
			; but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῆς ὁρτῆς τῇ
			δορπίῃ</span> on the <i>eve</i> of the feast, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.48
			</span></i>.</div>
